# 🧱 PNJC Core Contracts Specification

## Overview

This document describes the functional behavior of all smart contracts within the PNJC ecosystem. It serves as a reference for auditors, integrators, and external reviewers.

All contracts are designed to be:
- Non-upgradeable
- Deterministic
- Minimal in attack surface
- Fully compatible with EVM standards

---

# 1. PNJC Token Contract

## Type
ERC-20 standard token with extensions.

## Interfaces
- ERC20
- ERC20Permit (EIP-2612)
- ERC20Burnable

## Behavior

### Supply
- Fixed total supply minted at deployment
- No minting function exists

### Transfers
- Standard ERC20 transfer logic
- No transfer fees
- No blacklist/whitelist logic

### Permissions
- No owner
- No admin role
- No privileged functions

### Extensions
- Permit: allows gasless approvals via signatures
- Burn: token holders may irreversibly burn tokens

---

# 2. Liquidity Locker Contract

## Purpose
Locks LP tokens until a predefined unlock timestamp.

## Behavior

### Locking
- LP tokens are locked at deployment or via initialization
- Locked amount is immutable after creation

### Withdrawal
- Only beneficiary can withdraw
- Withdrawal is allowed only after unlock timestamp
- Partial withdrawals are NOT allowed

### Security
- No admin override
- No emergency withdrawal
- No upgradeability

---

# 3. Vesting Vault Contract

## Purpose
Linear time-based token distribution.

## Behavior

### Vesting Logic
- Linear vesting over fixed duration
- Starts at predefined timestamp
- Ends at full allocation release

### Claims
- Only beneficiary can claim
- Claimable amount = vested - already claimed
- Claims are incremental and irreversible

### Security
- No external modification of schedule
- No admin intervention
- No early unlock mechanism

---

# 4. Airdrop Contract

## Purpose
Merkle proof-based token distribution system.

## Behavior

### Claim Process
- Each user must provide valid Merkle proof
- Each address can claim only once
- Claims are final and irreversible

### Validation
- Leaf = hash(account, amount)
- Proof must match stored Merkle root

### Security
- No admin override
- No manual claim insertion
- No post-deployment changes to root

---

# 5. Treasury (Multisig Wallet)

## Type
External multisig wallet (off-chain governed)

## Behavior

### Funds
- Receives ecosystem funds
- Used for operational expenses

### Control
- Controlled by multisig signers
- No on-chain governance enforcement
- No smart contract logic beyond basic transfer

---

# 6. Global Security Properties

Across all contracts:

- No upgradeability
- No proxy patterns
- No admin backdoors
- No hidden minting
- Deterministic execution only
- Fully EVM-compatible behavior

---

# 7. Integration Notes

External protocols interacting with PNJC should assume:

- Standard ERC20 compliance
- No dynamic fees or taxes
- No blacklisting behavior
- Immutable supply constraints

